Description: pvr, pco: load small uniform buffers into shared registers
 pco reads only push constants and inline uniform blocks from shared
 registers; every other uniform buffer load is a memory load with a wait
 in each instance. zink puts all GL uniforms (constant buffer 0) into a
 plain uniform buffer, so every GL shader with uniforms pays that.
 .
 pco_nir_lower_io() now picks up to PCO_MAX_PROMOTED_UBOS uniform buffers
 whose loads all have constant descriptors, constant 4-byte aligned
 offsets and 32-bit results, PCO_MAX_PROMOTED_UBO_DWORDS dwords in total,
 for vertex and fragment shaders without robust buffer access. Bindings
 with update-after-bind or update-unused-while-pending are excluded,
 because the driver reads the descriptor when recording. The loads read
 the shared registers like an inline uniform block, and the null check of
 such a descriptor folds to false.
 .
 The PDS descriptor program DMAs each range into its shared registers
 (PVR_BUFFER_TYPE_UBO, which pvr_pds.h already had). At draw time the
 driver reads the buffer descriptor from the bound set, writes its address
 and sets the DMA size to the smaller of the promoted range and the bound
 range, so the DMA never reads past the range. A null descriptor gets a
 zero-filled upload instead.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
